    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d739">

                <pb facs="1032" n="912" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg912"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2654: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="81"
                        xml:id="d739-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-23T17:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1922—5 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 23—9:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>349. Your 205, August 21, 3 p.m.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d739-f2"/> Assertion of
                    China’s unique interest in railway as located on Chinese territory, claim that
                    agreement of Chinese Government with Russo-Asiatic Bank determines present
                    status of the railway, insistence on right of China exclusive of all other
                    nations to administer railway till Russia is recognized and negotiations with
                    Russia when recognized for final settlement of the matter. Demand dissolution of
                    Technical Board as soon as Japanese forces withdraw from Siberia.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d739-f1" n="81" type="source" xml:id="d739-f1-content">
                <p>Last sentence added as requested by the Minister in his telegram no. 350 of Aug.
                    24 (not printed).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d739-f2" n="82" xml:id="d739-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; it requested a brief outline of China’s program for the Chinese
                    Eastern Railway.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
